pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Regression test (wrong verdict): three lines refuted a tautology. `1 x1 >= 0`
% is satisfied by every assignment, and this proof used to be accepted as
% `s VERIFIED UNSATISFIABLE` at exit 0 with default flags.
%
% Two bugs stacked. `SubproofContext::pop_database_goal` answered `proofgoal 1`
% inside a `pbc` -- a subproof that owes NO database obligations at all -- by
% inventing a goal out of the database constraint itself, which is discharged
% for free because its counterexample premise contradicts the very database it
% is proven against. `EndSubproofChecker::end_proofgoal` then set
% `contradiction_proven` on the enclosing subproof for ANY discharged goal
% whenever that subproof was a proof by contradiction, and
% `SubproofContext::finalize` treats that flag as licence to skip every
% remaining obligation AND the top-level RUP check. So `pbc` never had to show
% its contradiction and happily added `>= 1`.
%
% `contradiction_proven` may now only be set for a goal whose counterexample
% premises the negated conclusion already entails (see
% `rules::proofgoal::discharges_pbc_contradiction`), and a database proofgoal
% is only reconstructed for a subproof that owes database obligations.
f 1;
pbc >= 1 : subproof
  proofgoal 1
    pol -1 1 +;
  qed;
qed;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
